Task temporal-101
SQLite schema:
CREATE TABLE accounts_101(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, active INTEGER); CREATE TABLE events_101(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, account_id INTEGER, at INTEGER, state TEXT);
Obligations: For EVERY active account, return id and the state of its latest event with at <= 5; ties in at are broken by the greatest event id. If it has no eligible event use the text NONE. Inactive accounts are excluded. Events after the cutoff must not affect selection. Order by account id.
Public example data: {"accounts_101": [[1, 1], [2, 1], [3, 1], [4, 1], [5, 1], [6, 1], [7, 1], [8, 0], [9, 1]], "events_101": [[1, 2, 1, "open"], [2, 2, 5, "closed"], [3, 2, 5, "open"], [4, 2, 6, "closed"], [5, 3, 1, "paused"], [6, 3, 5, "open"], [7, 3, 5, "paused"], [8, 3, 6, "paused"], [9, 4, 1, "open"], [10, 4, 5, "open"], [11, 4, 5, "closed"], [12, 4, 6, "closed"], [13, 5, 1, "paused"], [14, 5, 5, "open"], [15, 5, 5, "paused"], [16, 5, 6, "open"], [17, 6, 1, "open"], [18, 6, 5, "paused"], [19, 6, 5, "paused"], [20, 6, 6, "closed"], [21, 7, 1, "open"], [22, 7, 5, "closed"], [23, 7, 5, "paused"], [24, 7, 6, "paused"], [25, 8, 1, "paused"], [26, 8, 5, "paused"], [27, 8, 5, "closed"], [28, 8, 6, "closed"], [29, 9, 1, "open"], [30, 9, 5, "closed"], [31, 9, 5, "open"], [32, 9, 6, "open"]]}
Write a reusable SQL query valid for all databases satisfying this schema and obligations, not just these example rows.
